## Result

Status: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS

The v16 design retake removes the 22-destination home bounce. All 26 current navigation destinations now have a unique route, unique screen identity and current-owner behavior. Marketing Agent is additive customer guidance from brand facts through the next experiment. Studio, provider families, Inbox, Calendar, assets and Settings retain their current ownership.

## Files

- `DESIGN.md`, v16 section: brand adjectives, tokens, component inventory, state contract, 26-route contract and forbidden patterns
- `docs/user-flow-marketing-agent-v16-gpt-codex.md`: happy, edge, empty, error, loading, uncertain and repair paths with dead-end audit
- `docs/wireframes/marketing-agent-v16-gpt-codex.md`: responsive core screens, 26-route family behavior and role-aware Settings
- `docs/prototype/openclaw-auto-marketing-agent-fidelity-v16-gpt-codex.html`: self-contained clickable 1440, 1024 and 390 hub with state, role, theme and drawer controls

## Benchmark evidence and adaptation

Web search and source-page review were completed before final design decisions.

- Buffer Post Groups: retained per-post edit, delete, reschedule and publish independence inside grouped work.
- Sprout Social Message Approval: retained Needs Approval, edit, activity, reject and resubmit semantics while adding exact account, content, time and channel truth.
- Later multi-profile scheduling: retained per-profile customization and independent results while making unsupported capabilities explicit.
- Later Social Sets: adapted identity grouping into visible workspace account, handle, connection status and `verified_at`.
- Hootsuite approval: retained approval as a visible control point, but avoided implying that one approval covers changed content or destinations.

